# Invisible asteroids — no body at all, only the gravitational lens they
# bend the starfield through (WarpPass). The whole effect is motion: a still
# of this reads as an empty field, which is exactly why it's a clip.
#
# Two things this scene learned the hard way:
#  - The lens is a SCREEN-SPACE radial warp with no outline of its own, so it
#    only reads against dense stars (`stars 1.0`) at a big on-screen radius
#    (r=240 is Asteroid::max_radius). Zoomed far out it vanishes entirely.
#  - Keep them off the ship. A big rock that reaches the spawn kills the
#    pilot and sheds VISIBLE fragments, which gives the trick away — that is
#    what the white outlines in the first cut of this scene actually were.
#    Note the ship cannot be moved out of the way to arrange that: the camera
#    IS player 1, so `ship` slides the whole view with it. Leave the ship at
#    the origin and route the rocks past it (|y| > r + ship radius) instead.
seed 21
sim 300
frames 90
fps 30
size 960 540
clear
hud off
camera fixed
zoom 55
stars 1.0
ship 0 0 0
asteroid -780 330 invisible r=240 v=230,0
asteroid 780 -330 invisible r=240 v=-230,0
